DEFERRED -- DO NOT APPLY. This makes things WORSE than not having it.

SHORT-CIRCUIT && AND ||, which C requires and micro-c does not do. It emits a
bitwise AND of both operands instead, so

    if (esym && esym->st_shndx == SHN_UNDEF)

dereferences esym even when it is null. tcc has FORTY-EIGHT of those.

THIS IS A REAL BUG AND THIS IS A REAL FIX FOR IT, AND APPLYING IT TODAY IS
STILL WRONG. Measured, on the same source, with and without:

    without   libtcc.c compiles in 42s, 351,497 lines
              the built tcc reaches tcc_set_output_type (markers to T9)

    with      libtcc.c is OOM-KILLED at 38s in a 4 GB container
              in CI, where memory is not the limit, the built tcc dies
              INSIDE tcc_new -- earlier than any point reached since the
              instruction-alignment bug

So it costs a large amount of memory AND moves the failure backwards. Two
theories were tried and neither was it:

  1. The far-jump helper reaches its label through x16, which is
     REGISTER_TEMP -- and micro-c's CALL SEQUENCE holds the callee's new base
     pointer there between mov_x16,x18 and mov_x17,x16. A && inside an
     ARGUMENT LIST would destroy the callee's frame. That is a genuine hazard
     and if/while never hit it because they branch at STATEMENT level where
     x16 is dead.

     Saving and restoring x16 around the sequence -- included here, verified
     as one push and one pop -- did NOT fix the fault.

  2. The memory growth suggested something unbounded in label generation.
     Each operator allocates two ids; that is small, and does not explain
     hundreds of megabytes.

WHAT IS LEFT TO CHECK, for whoever picks this up:

  - whether emit_jump_if_zero clobbers anything besides x16
  - whether current_target is left wrong: general_recursion goes through
    common_recursion, which ends with promote_type; this helper does not, so
    the type after a && is whatever the right operand left
  - where the memory actually goes -- measure it rather than reasoning about
    it, which is what the two failed theories above did

The honest summary is that the diagnosis stopped short. The fix is kept
because the bug it addresses is real and will have to be fixed before tcc can
work, and because the next attempt should start from what was already tried.

